course: dictionary
lesson: 9186
title: Sociable: getting on with others
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sociable is a describing word. It means liking to meet and talk with other people, and being friendly. A sociable person enjoys company, and a sociable place or event is one where people mix and get along.
explain: The clues around the word help you. «The class party was sociable, with music, games and chatting in every corner.» Music, games and chatting show people mixing and relaxed, so sociable means friendly and relaxed. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: Sociable can also describe animals. «Meerkats are sociable and live in big groups.» Living in groups tells you the word is about getting on well with others. Sociable hours are a different use: normal working times, the opposite of unsociable hours like nights.
fact: Sociable means liking to meet and talk with other people; friendly.
fact: «A sociable evening» means a friendly, relaxed event where people mix.
fact: Sociable animals live and get on well in groups, like dolphins, meerkats and bees.
fact: «Sociable hours» are normal working times, the opposite of unsociable hours like nights.
fact: Sociable weavers in the Kalahari build giant shared nests with over 100 birds; the thick straw keeps them cool by day and warm on freezing desert nights.
exercise: «The sociable dog wagged its tail at everyone who came to the park.» What does sociable mean here? | *Friendly, and happy to be with others | Asleep all day | Very fast | Scared of people
exercise: «It was a sociable evening, with games and chatting in every corner.» What kind of evening was it? | *Friendly and relaxed, where people mix | Silent and dark | Cold and wet | Only for grown-ups
exercise: «Sociable weavers in the Kalahari build giant shared nests.» Which word shows that the birds build together? | Straw | *Shared | Desert | Trees
test: «The new girl was sociable and talked to everyone at lunch.» What does sociable mean? | Angry at lunch | Bored of food | *Friendly and happy to talk with others | Tired and quiet
test: Which of these is a sociable animal that lives in groups? | Pencil | *Dolphin | Stone | Lamp
exam: «Sociable hours» are normal working times. What is the opposite of sociable hours? | Weekends with games | Lunch breaks | *Unsociable hours, like nights | Sociable evenings
